---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Choose Your Own Adventure | WDD 231"
  description="A competency-based learning path for WDD 231 Web Frontend Development I."
>
  <article>
    <h1>Choose Your Own Adventure</h1>

    <p class="lead">
      WDD 231 is becoming a more student-directed course. Instead of requiring
      everyone to complete the same sequence of assignments, you will choose
      meaningful work that helps you develop and demonstrate the course
      competencies.
    </p>

    <p>
      You choose the project, resources, practice activities, and sometimes the
      order in which you work. The course still provides clear outcomes,
      checkpoints, feedback, and evidence requirements so that independence does
      not mean working without direction.
    </p>

    <h2>How the approach works</h2>

    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>Choose a focus.</strong> Select a competency or a small group of related
        competency slices that fit your current needs and interests.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Make a learning contract.</strong> Describe what you will learn, how
        you will practice, what support you need, and what evidence will demonstrate
        your progress.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Build and investigate.</strong> Use the resources that fit your starting
        point. Create a working increment, test it, and document what you discover.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Show your learning.</strong> Demonstrate the work, explain your decisions,
        respond to a small variation, and use feedback to choose your next step.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2>What stays consistent</h2>

    <p>
      Your path may be different from another student's path, but the standard
      for meaningful learning remains consistent. Strong evidence usually
      includes a working artifact, an explanation of important decisions, a
      verification or test, and a discussion of one problem, limitation, or
      tradeoff. You should be able to explain and adapt the work rather than
      simply show that it runs.
    </p>

    <h2>Start here</h2>

    <ul class="resources">
      <li>
        <a href={import.meta.env.BASE_URL + "/ponder/learning-contract/"}>
          Create a Learning Contract
        </a>
        <span>— Write a focused plan for your next learning increment.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          href={import.meta.env.BASE_URL +
            "/ponder/model-first-learning-contract/"}
        >
          Model the First Learning Contract
        </a>
        <span>— See a fully completed example for the first shared week.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          href={import.meta.env.BASE_URL +
            "/ponder/recommended-11-contract-path/"}
        >
          Recommended 10-Contract Path
        </a>
        <span
          >— Follow a suggested 10-contract sequence if you are unsure what to
          do next.</span
        >
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={import.meta.env.BASE_URL + "/resources/competencies/"}>
          WDD 231 Competency Guide
        </a>
        <span>— Review the skills, evidence, and proficiency descriptions.</span
        >
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={import.meta.env.BASE_URL + "/ponder/competency-pass-off/"}>
          Pass Off a Competency or Slice
        </a>
        <span
          >— Prepare for the peer conversation and instructor or TA
          demonstration.</span
        >
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Remember</h2>

    <p>
      You are responsible for choosing a useful next step, asking for help when
      you need it, and producing honest evidence of what you can do. Your
      instructor's role is to help you set an appropriate scope, connect you
      with resources, challenge your understanding, and confirm your progress.
    </p>

    <h2>Grading</h2>
    <p>
      You should treat this course as a pass/fail course. To pass the course,
      you must pass off all of the required competencies or slices at Proficient
      or better. This will earn you a B in the course. In order to get an A you
      must either demonstrate Advanced mastery on 4 or more competencies or pass
      off competency 9 at Proficient or higher (Performance and deployment).
    </p>
  </article>

  <style>
    article {
      max-width: 760px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 1rem;
    }

    h1 {
      margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }

    h2 {
      margin-top: 2rem;
    }

    .lead {
      font-size: 1.2rem;
    }

    li {
      margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    }

    .resources {
      padding-left: 1.25rem;
    }

    .resources a {
      font-weight: 700;
    }

    .resources span {
      display: block;
      margin-top: 0.15rem;
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
